# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values.
# Never commit .env.local to version control.

# ─── Supabase (public) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─── Supabase (server-only) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
AUTH_SECRET=

# ─── App Config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# The canonical public URL. Used by sitemap.ts, robots.ts, and OG tags.
# Set to https://theblacqlist.com in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ─── Coming-soon gate (pre-launch) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# When COMING_SOON_MODE=true, the public is redirected to /coming-soon. Visit
# /?preview=<token> once to bypass (sets a cookie); an authenticated session also
# bypasses. Flip to false (or unset) + redeploy to open the full site at launch.
# BYPASS_TOKEN is a secret — set a long random value; never commit a real one.
COMING_SOON_MODE=false
COMING_SOON_BYPASS_TOKEN=

# ─── Map tiles (self-hosted PMTiles) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# BOTH are optional. A fresh clone renders the basemap with neither set, because
# each one falls back:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES_URL   unset -> components/map/MapExplore.tsx falls back
#                               to `${window.location.origin}/api/map/tiles`
#   MAP_TILES_UPSTREAM_URL      unset -> app/api/map/tiles/route.ts falls back to
#                               ${NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL}/storage/v1/object/
#                               public/map-tiles/blacqlist-metros.pmtiles
#
# So the default path is: browser -> our own /api/map/tiles -> the public
# Supabase Storage object. That indirection is deliberate, not incidental —
# Supabase Storage does not expose Content-Range in Access-Control-Expose-Headers,
# so a browser reading the archive cross-origin silently stalls the pmtiles
# client. The same-origin proxy removes CORS from the equation.
#
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES_URL only when pointing the client at an archive that
# DOES expose range headers cross-origin (a CDN). Set MAP_TILES_UPSTREAM_URL only
# when the archive lives somewhere other than this project's `map-tiles` bucket.
#
# Prerequisite for the default path: the `map-tiles` bucket must exist and be
# PUBLIC on the Supabase project this environment points at. If it is private,
# the proxy returns 502 and the map renders without a basemap.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES_URL=
MAP_TILES_UPSTREAM_URL=

# ─── Email (Resend) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=
ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=

# ─── Stripe ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keys from Stripe Dashboard -> Developers -> API keys
# Use TEST keys locally; LIVE keys in production only
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Webhook secret: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# One-time price for a single 30-day job posting, sold to owners who are out of
# included postings (E-2 Model C). A recurring price will NOT work — the checkout
# session is created in `mode: 'payment'`. Unset means job checkout is refused
# outright (`jobPostingPriceId()` returns null), never silently free.
STRIPE_JOB_POSTING_PRICE_ID=

# ─── Feature flags ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Parsed by lib/env.ts. On: 1/true/on/yes/enabled. Off: 0/false/off/no/disabled.
# Anything else is ignored, not treated as on. When a flag is unset or
# unrecognized it defaults to ON everywhere except
# production, so a missing var never turns something on for real users.
# The full flag list lives in `FEATURE_FLAG_ENV_VARS` in lib/env.ts.
#
# paidPostings gates the whole E-2 monetization path: job checkout, the included
# job allowance, event caps, and the job half of the nightly expiry sweep. Off in
# production until the Stripe price above exists at every Vercel scope.
FEATURE_PAID_POSTINGS=

# postingSubmissions gates the /add-event and /add-job forms and the event/job
# half of createListingAction. Both forms work and are auth-gated, but nothing
# links to them and nothing renders or moderates what they write. Off in
# production until events and jobs have a surface and a moderation path. Does
# NOT gate the public /events and /jobs beta pages or their waitlist capture.
FEATURE_POSTING_SUBMISSIONS=

# ─── Scheduled jobs (Vercel Cron) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The schedule itself is versioned in `vercel.ts` (/api/cron/expiry, 08:00 UTC
# daily). This is the shared secret the route checks against the incoming
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` header.
#
# The route fails CLOSED: unset returns 503 and runs no sweeps, because it holds
# the service role and unpublishes listings. Any long random value; must match
# what the caller sends. ⚠ Production currently has this UNSET — that is why the
# expiry cron 503s today (§2C1).
CRON_SECRET=

# ─── Sentry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=

# ─── Meta Graph API (Instagram + Facebook) — ops social tooling ──────────────
# Used by lib/meta/ and scripts/meta/* (social-listening + social-content agents).
# One-time setup: docs/blacqlist/ops/runbooks/meta-setup.md
# App ID + Secret are only needed to run scripts/meta/exchange-token.ts.
META_APP_ID=
META_APP_SECRET=
# The Facebook Page ID and the linked Instagram Business/Creator account ID.
META_PAGE_ID=
META_IG_BUSINESS_ID=
# Long-lived Page access token (from exchange-token.ts). Secret — never commit.
META_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Graph API version (optional; defaults to v22.0).
META_GRAPH_VERSION=v22.0

# ─── Coming-soon rate limiter ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Salt for the pseudonymized client IP stored by the /coming-soon capture
# throttle (lib/actions/subscribers/subscribeLaunch.ts → launch_subscribe_attempts).
# A bare sha256 of an IP is trivially reversible — the whole IPv4 space is only
# 4 billion hashes — so this salt is what makes the stored digest non-identifying.
# Any long random string. If unset, the limit is STILL enforced with an unsalted
# hash; only the pseudonymization strength degrades.
SUBSCRIBE_RATE_LIMIT_SALT=

# ─── Cloudflare Turnstile (CAPTCHA) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Protects sign-up, sign-in, password reset, claims, and reviews.
# Create a widget at dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile and add the site domains.
#
# ⚠ A SITE KEY AND A SECRET ARE A MATCHED PAIR. Cloudflare issues them together
# per widget, and a token minted by one site key can only be verified by its own
# secret. Mixing pairs does not degrade — it fails CLOSED, on every attempt, with
# no useful error. That is the whole reason for the per-scope table below.
#
# There are TWO enforcement paths with TWO different secret stores, and only one
# of them is this app's:
#
#   surface                          token verified by   secret lives in
#   /sign-up /sign-in /forgot-*      SUPABASE            the Supabase dashboard,
#                                    Attack Protection   per project
#   claim form, review form          this app            TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
#                                    (verifyTurnstileFormData)
#
# Staging's Supabase project holds the always-pass TEST secret; production holds
# the REAL one. So the site key served to a Preview or to local dev — both of
# which talk to staging — must be the TEST site key, or sign-in is impossible
# there. Serving one real site key to every scope is what broke Preview and local
# auth for weeks (debt ⑫, fixed 2026-09-02).
#
# Scope them in Vercel exactly like this:
#
#   variable                          Production   Preview   Development
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY    real         test      test
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY              real         test      UNSET
#
# Development leaves the SECRET unset on purpose. These two keys have no fallback
# chain, so a scope they are missing from simply degrades: the widget renders
# nothing and the server-side check is skipped. That is exactly what CI does
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml) and it is what keeps local dev working without a
# Cloudflare credential. Contrast NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL, which DOES have a fallback
# chain (lib/env.ts — explicit ?? VERCEL_URL ?? localhost): it belongs at
# Production ONLY, because a Preview-scoped value would override the correct
# per-deployment VERCEL_URL.
#
# Enable CAPTCHA on BOTH Supabase projects — Authentication -> Attack Protection
# — pasting the matching secret into each: the TEST secret at staging, the REAL
# one at production. /auth/v1/signup is reachable directly with the anon key, so
# an app-side check alone would protect nothing.
#
# Locally, put the TEST site key in .env.local and leave the secret out. Without
# it e2e/helpers/auth.ts times out and the authenticated Playwright specs fail:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
#
# Cloudflare's always-pass test keys (safe to commit, use in CI):
#   site   1x00000000000000000000AA
#   secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
